// Package orchestrator is the packaged-playback POLICY core (D-8/D-9): the
// watch-driven packaging frontier, the movie pack-on-play decision, and the
// storage-budget accounting with LRU eviction — pure functions over narrow
// input snapshots that RETURN decisions.
//
// Invariants (the whole package, no exceptions):
//
//   - Policy only. This package NEVER executes ffmpeg (never touches
//     os/exec), NEVER writes item documents, and NEVER touches library
//     directories. The composition root (cmd/mellifera) executes the
//     returned decisions: jobs ride enrich.Queue.EnqueuePack, evicted
//     artifact paths are moved to a .trash sibling and deleted, and every
//     store read is passed IN as data.
//   - Pure core. Every exported function is deterministic over its inputs
//     (time enters as an argument — FrontierIn.Now, the Evictions clock —
//     never as a clock read), mutates nothing, and reads nothing but its
//     arguments. Tests are therefore plain table-driven calls.
//   - Narrow inputs. Serial/Episode/ArtifactDir carry exactly the facts the
//     policies judge (canonical episode order, packaging state, cooldown,
//     disk truth); classification, cooldown deadlines, and disk sizes are
//     computed by the caller from the store and the artifact root.
//   - The direct floor is invisible here by construction: nothing in this
//     package can make an item unplayable — the frontier merely chooses
//     what to package, and eviction only ever reaps artifact directories
//     (originals are never an input).
//
// Exported surface (≤8): Frontier, FrontierIn, Serial, Episode, Job,
// OnPlay, Evictions, ArtifactDir.
package orchestrator

import "time"

// Packaging-state eligibility is the ONE rule both enqueue paths share
// (spec "Watch-driven packaging frontier"): an item is enqueued only when
// its classification permits packaging, nothing is published for it yet,
// and it is outside its packaging failure cooldown. Unexported: callers
// never re-implement the gate.
func eligible(e Episode, now time.Time) bool {
	return e.Packable && !e.Packaged && !e.CoolUntil.After(now)
}
